      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1197532476">
          <groundspeak:date>2023-09-27T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP529 Three Hills 2 [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Up here for some high school volleyball tonight and decided to attempt this before heading back. Still a pretty easy find in the divot. TFTBC. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="1006066311">
          <groundspeak:date>2021-04-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="181446">DanOCan</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP529 Three Hills 2 [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Upon arriving in Three Hills, this was the first stop.  I have two caps to find in town and I foolishly figured I would find the second one on the way back through town but then we didn't end up coming back this way so I still have one left here.  Oh well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It took a couple minutes to locate this one.  Being below ground level and with more than three years since the last find, it had gotten pretty well covered back up.  After reviewing some previous logs and seeing the context photos, the hole was soon spotted and I set about digging.  I used one of Mabel's bags and faked like I was picking up after her so I [hopefully] didn't draw too much attention from the passing cars.  After getting my photos I kicked my little pile of dirt back in the hole so it wasn't obvious I had been digging in the grass.  Still should be an easy find for those following in my footsteps, providing they aren't afraid of getting their hands a little dirty to spot the brass.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
